reasoning=[
('o2','Six independent endpoint scalar constraints need six coefficients. With distinct endpoint times a fifth-degree Hermite interpolant exists uniquely; degree n has n+1 coefficients, so degrees 2, 3 and 4 cannot fit arbitrary six data.'),
('o3','At t=2 s the two remaining constraints are 4a2+8a3=1 rad and 4a2+12a3=0 rad/s after evaluating derivative units consistently. Subtracting the numerical equations gives a3=-0.25 rad/s^3, then a2=0.75 rad/s^2. The constant/linear coefficients are zero from initial rest at zero position.'),
('o4','Left and right velocity limits at 1 s both equal 1 m/s; the ordinary blend joins them continuously. The one-sided derivatives are respectively 1 m/s^2 and 0, so acceleration jumps and is not classically defined at the junction without an endpoint convention. Neither nonzero cruise speed nor velocity continuity implies continuous acceleration.'),
('o1','The angular displacement to the equivalent target is 340+360k degrees. k=-1 gives -20 degrees, the least absolute displacement. +340 reaches the target after the long rotation; +180 and -350 do not reach it from 10 degrees.'),
('o2','Small repeated spread establishes repeatability. The cluster center is 4 mm off the command, which is a systematic accuracy error, not evidence of scattered repeated endpoints or exact accuracy.'),
('o3','The law of cosines gives r^2=5^2+4^2+2*5*4*cos(theta2), hence r in [1,9] m. Only 0.5 m is below the folded lower bound; 1,5 and 9 m are reachable under unrestricted joints and no obstacles.'),
('o4','For a rank-six map from seven joint velocities, rank-nullity gives dimension ker(J)=7-6=1. The direction is instantaneous task-preserving, not a guarantee of arbitrary global obstacle-free self-motion.'),
('o1','Accurate joint angles do not measure bending of a compliant link. Adding load-dependent elastic deflection or measuring deformation addresses the missing physics; repeating rigid geometry, inferring exact position from encoders, or relabeling coordinates does not.'),
('o2','The source assembly role requires horizontal/lateral compliance so an insertion can accommodate small planar errors, while vertical stiffness supports the load. Reversing the directions or making all directions uniformly stiff/soft loses selective compliance.'),
('o3','Positive link lengths do not vanish, so determinant zero is equivalent to sin(theta2)=0: 0 or 180 degrees modulo 360. Both extended and folded alignment qualify; 45/225 and 90/270 do not.')]
